msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:6
#: fadd673760194fe89c5f8b2134d9dc29
msgid ""
"Qubes VMs have some settings set by dom0 based on that VM's settings. There "
"are multiple configuration channels, including:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:8
#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:19
#: 17821e4896044c39a946d05ccc82ba1f fad3d15fa17449899c1b3ac8fe30939c
msgid "QubesDB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:10
#: a099beeddc7b41a5b87eb912fa12a4dd
msgid ""
"XenStore (in Qubes 2, data the same as in QubesDB, keys without leading ``/"
"``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:12
#: e9294e7495584b34ab3cf9ef274e7139
msgid "Qubes RPC (called at VM startup, or when configuration changed)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:14
#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:295
#: a8bb9565c26c447cb90abec4a432be14 80e1aec4202b4f2081317fa0830ce279
msgid "GUI protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:23
#: f7a442681633498e9b19e6d07165cc66
msgid "Keys exposed by dom0 to VM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:26
#: 86809bed3ab1446194da9fbc1f397b7e
msgid "``/qubes-base-template`` - base template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:28
#: 0a66501367ca4bdba447ae8d22682156
msgid ""
"``/qubes-vm-type`` - VM type, the same as the ``type`` field in ``qvm-"
"prefs``. One of ``AppVM``, ``ProxyVM``, ``NetVM``, ``TemplateVM``, ``HVM``, "
"``TemplateHVM``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:30
#: 57c36592f1e04effb8f171fb4c8c31c7
msgid ""
"``/qubes-vm-updatable`` - flag indicating whether the VM is updatable "
"(whether changes in root.img will survive VM restart). One of ``True``, "
"``False``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:32
#: 623e459086764cfeb6245c2eea6867fa
msgid "``/qubes-vm-persistence`` - what data do persist between VM restarts:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:34
#: 5d1fd7389a114be3bb6fc4536beb4930
msgid "``full`` - all disks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:36
#: ef79ba5e09bf42dda41ebb1c1250334b
msgid "``rw-only`` - only ``/rw`` disk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:38
#: 1dd10a4a97944a38a7ddbf9f945771cc
msgid "``none`` - nothing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:42
#: 67304597aac5448f855d9a2697265681
msgid ""
"``/qubes-timezone`` - name of timezone based on dom0's timezone. Example: "
"``Europe/Warsaw``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:44
#: 94b4c2740a87432c894f49f364d9182a
msgid ""
"``/qubes-keyboard`` (deprecated in R4.1) - keyboard layout based on dom0's "
"layout. Its syntax is suitable for the ``xkbcomp`` command (after expanding "
"escape sequences like ``\\n`` or ``\\t``). This is meant only as some "
"default value, the VM can ignore this option and choose its own keyboard "
"layout (this is what the keyboard setting in Qubes Manager does). This entry "
"is created as part of gui-daemon initialization (it's not available when gui-"
"daemon is disabled, or has not started yet)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:46
#: fa6d211e667746bc96baa1bcf95d8622
msgid ""
"``/keyboard-layout`` - keyboard layout based on the GuiVM's layout. The "
"key's syntax can be ``layout+variant+options``, ``layout+variant``, ``layout+"
"+options`` or simply ``layout``. Example, ``fr+oss``, ``pl++compose:caps`` "
"or ``fr``. This is meant only as some default value, the VM can ignore this "
"option and choose its own keyboard layout (this is what the keyboard setting "
"in Qubes Manager does)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:48
#: 853e7da59a44438b905ca2b038f2585c
msgid ""
"``/qubes-debug-mode`` - flag indicating whether the VM has debug mode "
"enabled (qvm-prefs setting). One of ``1``, ``0``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:50
#: bd529e4d1ce14029b1691663adf49b0f
msgid ""
"``/qubes-service/SERVICE_NAME`` - subtree for VM services controlled from "
"dom0 (using the ``qvm-service`` command or Qubes Manager). One of ``1``, "
"``0``. Note that not every service will be listed here, if an entry is "
"missing, it means “use VM default”. A list of currently supported services "
"can be found in the ``qvm-service`` man page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:52
#: b872c54f838c4afb977589104edbacf4
msgid ""
"``/qubes-netmask`` - network mask (only when the VM has a netvm set); "
"currently hardcoded “255.255.255.0”"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:54
#: b144bb16376e42be9572e53bb73bc027
msgid ""
"``/qubes-ip`` - IP address for this VM (only when the VM has a netvm set)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:56
#: e90c0f5f3f6045d49a9338a793c813c2
msgid ""
"``/qubes-gateway`` - the default gateway's IP address (only when the VM has "
"a netvm set); VM should add a host route to this address directly via eth0 "
"(or whatever the default interface name is)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:58
#: a961cbe3315d4e0f8c94401d83d517d4
msgid ""
"``/qubes-primary-dns`` - primary DNS address (only when the VM has a netvm "
"set)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:60
#: 26b2bbfeafcd4f8c8e65730cadd4e339
msgid ""
"``/qubes-secondary-dns`` - secondary DNS address (only when the VM has a "
"netvm set)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:62
#: 62bbf1b9c268414f89d6999beb57eba4
msgid ""
"``/qubes-netvm-gateway`` - same as ``qubes-gateway`` in connected VMs (only "
"when VM serves as network backend - ProxyVM and NetVM)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:64
#: 50891da7ee6d428a9c3a52f1cbc05a7d
msgid ""
"``/qubes-netvm-netmask`` - same as ``qubes-netmask`` in connected VMs (only "
"when VM serves as network backend - ProxyVM and NetVM)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:66
#: 2e68745be6804ab3b711cd9366793711
msgid ""
"``/qubes-netvm-network`` - network address (only when VM serves as network "
"backend - ProxyVM and NetVM); can be also calculated from qubes-netvm-"
"gateway and qubes-netvm-netmask"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:68
#: a3f4afa97d554c41b725f3fd4c6e90e4
msgid ""
"``/qubes-netvm-primary-dns`` - same as ``qubes-primary-dns`` in connected "
"VMs (only when VM serves as network backend - ProxyVM and NetVM); traffic "
"sent to this IP on port 53 should be redirected to the primary DNS server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:70
#: ce1088c500304944ae935a8e1700c04d
msgid ""
"``/qubes-netvm-secondary-dns`` - same as ``qubes-secondary-dns`` in "
"connected VMs (only when VM serves as network backend - ProxyVM and NetVM); "
"traffic sent to this IP on port 53 should be redirected to the secondary DNS "
"server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:72
#: 82f3e799982945afa422443842983059
msgid ""
"``/guivm-windows-prefix`` - title prefix for any window not originating from "
"another qube. This means windows of applications running in the GuiVM itself"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:77
#: 796124c3107546d9a1d6a838a5304062
msgid "Firewall rules in 3.x"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:80
#: 45f31d64754d47d9b34c66941e87bbae
msgid ""
"QubesDB is also used to configure the firewall in ProxyVMs. Rules are stored "
"in separate keys for each target VM. Entries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:82
#: 0b7fb595eb3644fd82b655f762550bc8
msgid ""
"``/qubes-iptables`` - control entry - dom0 writing ``reload`` here signals "
"the ``qubes-firewall`` service to reload rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:84
#: d736ac3af0844fdf9ce5bfde7608b516
msgid ""
"``/qubes-iptables-header`` - rules not related to any particular VM, should "
"be applied before domain rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:86
#: b6aa424744d744739439c5dc51bd62ea
msgid ""
"``/qubes-iptables-domainrules/NNN`` - rules for domain ``NNN`` (arbitrary "
"number) in ``iptables-save`` format. Rules are self-contained - they fill "
"``FORWARD`` iptables chain and contain all required matches (source IP "
"address etc.), as well as a final default action (``DROP``/``ACCEPT``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:90
#: b7cd397f9cef4a11b52a021975b80006
msgid ""
"After applying the rules, the VM may signal some error, writing a message to "
"the ``/qubes-iptables-error`` key. This does not preclude any other way of "
"communicating problems, such as with a popup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:93
#: 4ec6af93785c4a299ccf89d655f0a260
msgid "Firewall rules in 4.x"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:96
#: 607e681c4ee548e086a56ea9d93f3479
msgid ""
"QubesDB is also used to configure the firewall in ProxyVMs. Each rule is "
"stored as a separate entry, grouped by target VMs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:98
#: bc78cc7a5b80497490f3f474425a50a6
msgid ""
"``/qubes-firewall/SOURCE_IP`` - base tree under which rules are placed. All "
"rules there should be applied to filter traffic coming from ``SOURCE_IP``. "
"This can be either an IPv4 or IPv6 address. Dom0 will do an empty write to "
"this top level entry after finishing an update of the rules, so the VM can "
"setup a watch here to trigger rules reload."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:100
#: ed9c87c2194b4fe2a4cdf9eb2cbc761e
msgid ""
"``/qubes-firewall/SOURCE_IP/policy`` - default action if no rule matches: "
"``drop`` or ``accept``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:102
#: c2376ab0eefd4f87a34a9518cd1d37a7
msgid ""
"``/qubes-firewall/SOURCE_IP/NNNN`` - rule number ``NNNN`` - decimal number, "
"padded with zeros. See below for rule format. All the rules should be "
"applied in the order of rules implied by those numbers. Note that QubesDB "
"itself does not impose any ordering (you need to sort the rules after "
"retrieving them). The first rule has the number ``0000``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:106
#: fc99776559894cf7aa9c3e5192f028a9
msgid ""
"Each rule is a single QubesDB entry, consisting of ``key=value`` pairs "
"separated by a space. QubesDB enforces a limit on a single entry's length - "
"3072 bytes. Possible options for a single rule:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:108
#: 97258589f726425fb48ce272bb52d839
msgid "``action``, values: ``accept``, ``drop``; this is present in every rule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:110
#: 941d72b04644423895e2e8c012175a3e
msgid ""
"``dst4``, value: destination IPv4 address with a mask; for example: "
"``192.168.0.0/24``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:112
#: ff93e02ef84c4e9cbc10b88b15e57681
msgid ""
"``dst6``, value: destination IPv6 address with a mask; for example: "
"``2000::/3``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:114
#: 815fa1bde77848f9aa80fb516147c063
msgid "``dsthost``, value: DNS hostname of the destination host"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:116
#: 249b77738c28435a9b81918bd2dadf0c
msgid "``proto``, values: ``tcp``, ``udp``, ``icmp``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:118
#: c7ec622445f041f0ad2b76c5192c38f9
msgid ""
"``specialtarget``, value: One of predefined target, currently defined values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:120
#: 87ff2ae0b2c046759af510be9cecf2c2
msgid ""
"``dns`` - such option should match DNS traffic to default DNS server (but "
"not any DNS server), on both TCP and UDP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:124
#: 919ee80b04db486c99b0327691d14ecc
msgid ""
"``dstports``, value: destination ports range separated with ``-``, valid "
"only together with ``proto=tcp`` or ``proto=udp``; for example ``1-1024``, "
"``80-80``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:126
#: 9da5a5f008974e67a4d227f256c9fb8c
msgid ""
"``icmptype``, value: numeric (decimal) icmp message type, for example ``8`` "
"for echo request, valid only together with ``proto=icmp``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:128
#: b181c5e285a6412bb0a4dc3b27935464
msgid ""
"``dpi``, value: Deep Packet Inspection protocol (like: HTTP, SSL, SMB, SSH, "
"SMTP) or the default ‘NO’ as no DPI, only packet filtering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:132
#: e94aefd98f5644129dbe267e26030a44
msgid ""
"Options must appear in the rule in the order listed above. Duplicated "
"options are forbidden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:134
#: a54e2c8106b5479ba62ca49ea3ecab31
msgid ""
"A rule matches only when all predicates match. Only one of ``dst4``, "
"``dst6`` or ``dsthost`` can be used in a single rule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:136
#: fcf23a0641a0476e83f014bc97864e55
msgid ""
"If the tool applying firewall rules encounters any parsing errors (unknown "
"option, invalid value, duplicated option, etc.), it should drop all the "
"traffic coming from that ``SOURCE_IP``, regardless of properly parsed rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:138
#: c9aff3e7d0fb4975a58b0a3f9948cd22
msgid "Example valid rules:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:140
#: 576812b9bbab40c8bb438311b6f752ab
msgid "``action=accept dst4=8.8.8.8 proto=udp dstports=53-53``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:142
#: 466aedb751244d6f98d6f777b6fb9d8f
msgid "``action=drop dst6=2a00:1450:4000::/37 proto=tcp``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:144
#: 19f581a9f2de464aaeb510d36795f473
msgid "``action=accept specialtarget=dns``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:146
#: d4304724386e466b91a60a1b87d724b4
msgid ""
"``action=drop proto=tcp specialtarget=dns`` - drop DNS queries sent using TCP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:148
#: fb307f3bdc04437abfd16fa6ff93f2ae
msgid "``action=drop``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:153
#: 450acf7fdd044f7fb440ba64b7d85fba
msgid "Keys set by VM for passing info to dom0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:156
#: 85a4789dd78b44cdb57d2483922e90d1
msgid ""
"``memory/meminfo`` (**xenstore**) - used memory (updated by qubes-meminfo-"
"writer), input information for qmemman;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:158
#: 60fe5f2b7f4c491291366d2a7053d006
msgid ""
"Qubes 3.x format: 6 lines (EOL encoded as ``\\n``), each in the format "
"“FIELD: VALUE kB”; fields: ``MemTotal``, ``MemFree``, ``Buffers``, "
"``Cached``, ``SwapTotal``, ``SwapFree``; meaning the same as in ``/proc/"
"meminfo`` on Linux."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:160
#: 3a6ad052b43440b28390d805ee8f4ac4
msgid "Qubes 4.0+ format: used memory size in the VM, in kbytes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:164
#: 8ca824194e6e4b33b0e870bedf08f924
msgid ""
"``/qubes-block-devices`` - list of block devices exposed by this VM, each "
"device (subdirectory) should be named in a way that VM can attach the device "
"based on the name. Each should contain these entries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:166
#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:176
#: d638469627ec40ab9bd4b1c31fb8a045 ecfd81414d2a4cdf996ccfc5a8f5cec6
msgid "``desc`` - device description (ASCII text)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:168
#: 4977003da50d4b9693abc3fadec9d9b8
msgid "``size`` - device size in bytes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:170
#: d1daed3a34ff4e639cc1f0b68e4f2bfa
msgid ""
"``mode`` - default connection mode; ``r`` for read-only, ``w`` for read-write"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:174
#: d3b0a4e294824fb282815785d3d0fd4f
msgid ""
"``/qubes-usb-devices`` - list of USB devices exposed by this VM, each device "
"(subdirectory) should contain:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:178
#: 62a2344db4d14851a1064dec49c44bf4
msgid "``usb-ver`` - USB version (1, 2 or 3)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:185
#: c015578681544689ab9366360c1b86b7
msgid "Qubes RPC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:188
#: 992beb737d3d4d0aac1e255e4a9fd575
msgid "Services called by dom0 to provide some VM configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:190
#: 4e6c9c0bc712497da7646d6b51a2ac11
msgid ""
"``qubes.SetMonitorLayout`` - provide a list of monitors (displays), one per "
"line. Each line contains four numbers: ``width height X Y width_mm "
"height_mm`` (physical dimensions - ``width_mm`` and ``height_mm`` - are "
"optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:192
#: aedc9b60be0b4c9a8e4088e6bebede1b
msgid "``qubes.WaitForSession`` - called to wait for full VM startup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:194
#: 89382003a95f494ab039ed3a0d307d10
msgid ""
"``qubes.GetAppmenus`` - receive appmenus from a given VM (template); TODO: "
"describe format here"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:196
#: 78b59a9e65a044129c15b865c8578a95
msgid "``qubes.GetImageRGBA`` - receive image/application icon. Protocol:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:198
#: 326d9cd9911b4b3e83f7493f7739e96d
msgid "Caller sends the name of the requested icon. This can be one of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:202
#: 4861e8f7982d4a92bd13f366df7c53de
msgid "``xdgicon:NAME`` - search for NAME in a standard icon theme"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:204
#: cf8bfd79c9064590a633c906de18afc8
msgid ""
"``-`` - get icon data from stdin (the caller), can be prefixed with format "
"name, for example ``png:-``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:206
#: 8aa0b21121524c438a644228c2c7e976
msgid "file name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:210
#: 1fda476cc0f54945b77cb8620783ed28
msgid ""
"The service responds with image dimensions: width and height as decimal "
"numbers, separated with a space and with an EOL marker at the end; then "
"image data in RGBA format (32 bits per pixel)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:216
#: 077a02e5b08948dbbe67f27a7c8b4e0d
msgid ""
"``qubes.SetDateTime`` - set the VM's clock, called periodically by dom0 (can "
"be triggered manually from dom0 by calling ``qvm-sync-clock``). The service "
"receives one line at stdin - time in the format of ``date -u -Iseconds``, "
"for example ``2015-07-31T16:10:43+0000``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:218
#: 50e217447b2941a8b1cf6b8871f11ebf
msgid ""
"``qubes.SetGuiMode`` - called in a HVM to switch between fullscreen and "
"seamless GUI mode. The service receives a single word on stdin - either "
"``FULLSCREEN`` or ``SEAMLESS``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:220
#: dda11dba93c04bf798a7a5191855fec5
msgid ""
"``qubes.ResizeDisk`` - called to inform that an underlying disk was resized. "
"Name of the disk image is passed on standard input (``root``, ``private``, "
"``volatile``, or other). This is used starting with Qubes 4.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:224
#: 76c6a2c804334dedb6ca00e58f3d5f70
msgid "Other qrexec services installed by default:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:226
#: e16361fa86e14f348a3c8fb933b5c76d
msgid ""
"``qubes.Backup`` - store a Qubes backup. The service receives a location "
"chosen by the user (one line, terminated by ``\\n``) and the backup archive "
"(:doc:`description of backup format </user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-"
"restore-v2>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:228
#: 8f3f6816e4554d9da7091e568b0a3e31
msgid ""
"``qubes.DetachPciDevice`` - service called in reaction to a ``qvm-pci -d`` "
"call on a running VM. The service receives one word - BDF of the device to "
"detach. When the service call ends, the device will be detached"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:230
#: 30139170e650447fbf3e6f52e4ef69a8
msgid ""
"``qubes.Filecopy`` - receive some files from another VM. Files sent in :doc:"
"`qfile format </developer/services/qfilecopy>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:232
#: fe538c2958f04dfdbc4abe78383fecef
msgid ""
"``qubes.OpenInVM`` - open a file in the called VM. Service receives a single "
"file on stdin (in :doc:`qfile format </developer/services/qfilecopy>`. After "
"a file viewer/editor is terminated, if the file was modified, it can be sent "
"back (just raw content, without any headers); otherwise service should just "
"terminate without sending anything. This service is used by both ``qvm-open-"
"in-vm`` and ``qvm-open-in-dvm`` tools. When called in a DispVM, service "
"termination will trigger DispVM cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:234
#: 015508aefc8b4f3187a153b48ba62a9d
msgid ""
"``qubes.Restore`` - retrieve a Qubes backup. The service receives the backup "
"location entered by the user (one line, terminated by ``\\n``). Afterwards, "
"it should output the backup archive in :doc:`qfile format </developer/"
"services/qfilecopy>` (core-agent-linux component contains the ``tar2qfile`` "
"utility to do the conversion)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:236
#: 9464ea8b160d4a71b737e0836dc1fbe0
msgid ""
"``qubes.SelectDirectory``, ``qubes.SelectFile`` - services which should show "
"the file/directory selection dialog and return (to stdout) a single line "
"containing the selected path, or nothing in the case of cancellation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:238
#: ccd1c5d35985480f98c32795090c41b0
msgid ""
"``qubes.SuspendPre`` - service called in every VM with a PCI device attached "
"just before system suspend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:240
#: 014a731e3a3540da8c51a275a3b3ea53
msgid ""
"``qubes.SuspendPost`` - service called in every VM with a PCI device "
"attached just after system resume"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:242
#: 1a0bd0f6c94349458f6e93355cb7d228
msgid ""
"``qubes.SyncNtpClock`` - service called to trigger network time "
"synchronization. Service should synchronize the local VM's time and "
"terminate when done."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:244
#: af4d2ef7e0c04745afb624fbd20bb92d
msgid ""
"``qubes.WindowIconUpdater`` - service called by the VM to send icons of "
"individual windows. The protocol there is simple one direction stream: VM "
"sends a window ID followed by an icon in ``qubes.GetImageRGBA`` format, then "
"the next window ID etc. VM can send an icon for the same window multiple "
"times to replace the previous one (for example for animated icons)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:246
#: 25780bc36d0f4ca886260bdd03ce8147
msgid ""
"``qubes.VMShell`` - call any command in the VM; the commands are passed one "
"per line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:248
#: 2518464dfccf4b79b595a1180a881683
msgid "``qubes.VMShell+WaitForSession`` waits for full VM startup first"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:252
#: d1ef285377a9424c9e3d44ffeac3c1ec
msgid ""
"``qubes.VMExec`` - call any command in the VM, without using a shell, the "
"command needs to be passed as argument and encoded as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:254
#: 25d863d63c614d0ebda8ca4e4557bff1
msgid "the executable name and arguments are separated by ``+``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:256
#: 865a182fc736445cb457fb1dc02bb287
msgid ""
"everything except alphanumeric characters, ``.`` and ``_`` needs to be "
"escaped"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:258
#: 4bb657fdb59a458c9c3939e395f76a60
msgid ""
"bytes are escaped as ``-HH`` (where ``HH`` is hex code, capital letters only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:260
#: cbdc9eb893f4454d9227694856959cd8
msgid "``-`` itself can be escaped as ``--``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:262
#: f2b60326599b43d3b45764bea7675c64
msgid ""
"example: to run ``ls -a /home/user``, use ``qubes.VMExec+ls+--"
"a+-2Fhome-2Fuser``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:266
#: ad699a5726af47a0a6b7bec002ba296b
msgid ""
"``qubes.VMExecGUI`` - a variant of ``qubes.VMExec`` that waits for full VM "
"startup first"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:270
#: 9fe3ab8de46547febafb84358e484a32
msgid "Services called in the GuiVM:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:272
#: 10e1a14ff1b742f58af5be008e4f9012
msgid ""
"``policy.Ask``, ``policy.Notify`` - confirmation prompts and notifications "
"for Qubes RPC calls, see :ref:`qrexec-policy implementation <developer/"
"services/qrexec-internals:\\`\\`qrexec-policy\\`\\` implementation>` for a "
"detailed description."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:276
#: fe6ba1060a7943ba86d32a106d9dcfdf
msgid ""
"Currently, Qubes still calls a few tools in VM directly, not using the "
"service abstraction. This will change in the future. Those tools are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:278
#: eb2415bcc0214fcca88be9bea668699f
msgid ""
"``/usr/lib/qubes/qubes-download-dom0-updates.sh`` - script to download "
"updates (or new packages to be installed) for dom0 (``qubes-dom0-update`` "
"tool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:280
#: b25d92e720fc495a977baead881c165b
msgid ""
"``date -u -Iseconds`` - called directly to retrieve time after calling the "
"``qubes.SyncNtpClock`` service (``qvm-sync-clock`` tool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:282
#: 137f1846c57c48e7a63e57d5a867bda6
msgid ""
"``nm-online -x`` - called before the ``qubes.SyncNtpClock`` service call by "
"the ``qvm-sync-clock`` tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:284
#: 08b450da127840c88095a755a319c06b
msgid ""
"``resize2fs`` - called to resize the filesystem on the /rw partition by the "
"``qvm-grow-private`` tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:286
#: 3a9bfbf36ba44c9e8761fa40a0531b27
msgid ""
"``gpk-update-viewer`` - called by Qubes Manager to display available updates "
"in a TemplateVM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:288
#: 7bbf1a6382fc4c92bb6662697f06d403
msgid ""
"``systemctl start qubes-update-check.timer`` (and similarly stop) - called "
"when enabling/disabling update checking in a given VM (``qubes-update-"
"check`` :doc:`qvm-service </user/advanced-topics/qubes-service>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:292
#: 264456a707ca4a5d88a51b2beba5f0fa
msgid ""
"Additionally, automatic tests extensively run various commands directly in "
"VMs. We do not plan to change that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/vm-interface.rst:298
#: d18ee74938884c5b882a3f805ed0b99a
msgid ""
"GUI initialization includes passing the whole screen dimensions from dom0 to "
"VM. This will most likely be overwritten by qubes.SetMonitorLayout Qubes RPC "
"call."
msgstr ""
